    library='''<p class="pg-kicker">One entry point for the full body of work</p><h1>Plans, resources and evidence.</h1><p class="pg-lead">Use the decision packet for the proposed pilot; use the evidence library to review provider policies, historical changes and alternatives. Earlier platform records carry their own checked dates and are not all reverified with each update.</p>'''+filters('libraryCards',[('all','All materials'),('plan','Pilot packet'),('compute','Compute & tools'),('continuity','Continuity'),('evidence','Research & talk')],True)+'''<div class="pg-grid" id="libraryCards">'''+catalog+'''<p class="pg-empty" hidden>No materials match. Clear the search or choose another category.</p></div><section><h2>Downloads for review and reuse</h2>'''+links([('Request PDF','cloudbank-access-request.pdf'),('Request text','cloudbank-access-request.txt'),('Pilot brief PDF','pilot-brief.pdf'),('Full pilot plan text','pilot-plan.txt'),('Default budget CSV','pilot-budget.csv'),('Pilot readiness CSV','pilot-readiness.csv'),('Program JSON','pilot-program.json'),('Evidence JSON','evidence.json'),('Federal map CSV','federal-compute.csv'),('Jetstream2 capacity CSV','classroom-capacity.csv')])+'''</section><section><h2>Three models, three scopes</h2><p>The talk’s 480-seat calculator illustrates college-scale demand. The route assessment models 80 seats on Jetstream2 with VM-specific SUs. This CloudBank request describes an 80-student CPU teaching pilot plus up to six staff identities; its initial student/shared data request is 440 GB before staff/overhead, with accounting and any expansion confirmed by CloudBank. These are different planning scenarios, not interchangeable provider budgets or awarded capacities.</p></section><section><h2>Reading the evidence correctly</h2><p>Current quota, loss of a benefit, new-account restriction, complete shutdown and a temporary access incident are different claims. Federal development funding, current operating support, state subsidy and an approved no-cost account are also different facts. Working storage and course hosting are separate from preservation.</p><p>Draft budgets, proposed tests and platform documentation do not establish actual classroom access, account limits or educational outcomes. Raw captures and the complete portable review archive stay in the local review folder; this public site contains reviewed outputs.</p></section>'''
